This ascension was conducted on the NAO nethack server for the 
tournament. I am a tile player so this required a lot of patience. But 
it paid off. I also managed to make the ascension without changing shape 
or polymorphing an object.

Thus far, this is also the highest-scoring wizard ascension, so I'm 
quite pleased :)

I descended to Sokoban and lost my kitten to a mordor orc on the Oracle 
level. Cleaned out Sokoban and found a spellbook of charm monster along 
the way. I went to minetown and made the priest mad when a magic missile 
bounced off a wall and hit him in the temple - but then charmed him and 
all the insects he summoned. The insects proceeded to attack anything 
that moved, including the guards (I love it when a plan comes together).

A word here about weapon enhancements for wizards: I must respectfully 
disagree with those who say that wizards shouldn't bother to enhance 
their quarterstaff skills. Unless you get an early Magicbane or have 
ridiculous amount of magic power then you must have some offensive 
capability while recouping power. If you never enhance quarterstaff 
skills you will be woefully vulnerable in the early/middlegame. It is 
better to survive now than to worry about what happens to wasted skill 
slots later.

So I opted for better survival. It paid off, although I admit some 
frustrations to not being able to use Magicbane as an expert later for 
some time. Still, survival is the #1 priority.

Minetown also gave me a magic lamp. I descended to the bottom of the 
mines, retrieved the luckstone and a spellbook of create monster, and 
came back to the altar. I blessed the lamp and got a wish (I used it on 
+2 silver dragon scale mail. Even though I had found an amulet of 
reflection in Sokoban. I could have used a bag of holding but I wanted 
the amulet slot later for an amulet of life saving). I resolved not to 
leave until my diety gave me Magicbane - a few thousand turns of saccing 
did the trick.

During this game I wound up enchanting Magicbane to +6. I usually leave 
it at +2 but I must say I prefer using it with a higher enchantment than 
with a lower one.

I returned to the main dungeon and proceeded down slowly. At level 11 
there was a neutral temple - and on level 12 a vault that had a portal 
to Ft. Ludios. Lovely! Gold out the ying yang and a handy temple with a 
priest! I opted to create carnage at the Fortress and get my AC down. I 
had several close calls but it was worth it, especially when I found an 
amulet of life saving. Magic missile is my friend :)

Along the way my level improved to 15 due to potions of gain level and 
wraith corpses. I decided to descend to the castle.

On level 16 a black pudding I killed dropped a tin wand. Hm...zap!

You may wish for an object...(do the happy dance!)

With some cool new equipment I got my AC to -22. Why not just do the 
quest now? So I completed the quest before getting to Medusa's island.

And it's a good thing I found that wand, because I got the varient of 
the island with a titan at the entrance. The titan threw a bolder at me 
and summoned a bunch of nasties, including a master lich, an olog-hai, 
and a winged gargoyle. I used a WoDigging and dug down to the next level.

The castle presented no significant issues. Killed the meddlesome 
guards, stole the second WoW and became nearly fairly powerful. Anhur 
decided to crown me on one of my back and forth visits to minetown, 
giving me a spellbook of FoD. The rest of the game presented no 
significant problems except for a wood nymph who stole my amulet of life 
saving on the way down (the wretch also put it on, so when I blasted her 
it fried the amulet and saved her neck...temporarily of course).

The ascension run was pretty trouble-free. I found the altar on the 
second try. The astral plane is a LOT easier when you have conflict and 
a c corpse in your gloved hand :)


